Root Cause Analysis:
The test failure is due to the `generateTag` function producing a tag that starts with "DOG-" instead of the expected "CATA-". The test expects the tag to match the pattern `/^CATA-/`, but the received string was "DOG-ML8RXVRB-R3A5". This indicates that the logic in the `generateTag` function is not correctly generating tags with the "CATA-" prefix.

File to Fix:
`src/utils/tagGenerator.ts`

Fixed Code:
```typescript
// src/utils/tagGenerator.ts

export function generateTag(): string {
    // Ensure the tag starts with the correct prefix "CATA-"
    const prefix = "CATA-";
    const randomPart = Math.random().toString(36).substring(2, 10).toUpperCase();
    const uniquePart = Math.random().toString(36).substring(2, 6).toUpperCase();
    return `${prefix}${randomPart}-${uniquePart}`;
}
```

